id: ops-b2bs
title: Confirm the daily release commits the rebuilt dist/ before its pack check
description: "The resumed-release heading branch changed daily-release.ts (the calendar-day heading helpers) without rebuilding the tracked dist/ output, and merging main carried main's dist forward. No PR-branch gate enforces dist parity: CI and the quick release gate rebuild before running tests and never compare against the committed build. The daily-release workflow's 'Pack verified release' step enforces parity only on main's release candidate, via git diff --exit-code -- . and the dist/ porcelain check after the release's own release:check build, so the first daily release after this merge would fail there until dist is rebuilt and committed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: "area:build","area:release"
created_at: "2026-11-17T08:17:21.282Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T06:06:45.665Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-17T08:19:43.995Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-17T08:19:43.995Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-claude
repro_steps: "Merge a PR that changes daily-release.ts without rebuilding the tracked dist/, then run the next daily release."
resolution: Confirmed planner-order defect. Decide release imports the checked-out tools dist/daily-release.js before the candidate build. Prepare now rebuilds the trusted tools checkout and fails on tracked dist drift before loading the planner.
expected_result: "The release rebuilds dist/, commits it in the release commit, and passes 'Pack verified release'."
